cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below. The frozen
  research record is commit cd03af9c, tag research-final
  (docs/RELEASE_PROVENANCE.md). Results are modeled, use proxy demand and are
  uncalibrated; the project is independent of COTA.
type: software
title: "COTA Transit Network Model and Optimization Harness"
version: 0.9.0
authors:
  - family-names: Gregory
    given-names: Ian
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ian-gregory94/cota-route-optimization"
abstract: >-
  A convergence-controlled optimization harness and working paper on how
  frequency allocation and network-design interventions trade off modeled
  unserved demand and passenger generalized cost on the Central Ohio Transit
  Authority (COTA) weekday bus network at approximately fixed modeled
  resources, with a frozen, provenance-tracked research record.
keywords:
  - transit network design
  - frequency setting
  - transit assignment
  - robustness analysis
  - reproducibility
  - Columbus, Ohio
references:
